If the vertical lines are \(x=1,\dots ,x=n-k\), then any point with \(x\le n-k\) is covered. For a point with \(x>n-k\) we have \(x=n-k+r\) with \(1\le r\le k\); the condition \(x+y\le n+1\) becomes \((n-k+r)+y\le n+1\), i.e. \(r+y\le k+1\). Setting \(x'=r\) and \(y'=y\) yields exactly the set \(T_k\). This reduction is correct **provided** the previous step is valid.

